- `ticks <int>` — total ticks to run, appears exactly once before actor directives
- `actor <id> <x> <y>` — create actor at position
- `moveby <id> <dx> <dy> <duration>` — queue MoveByAction on actor

The key detail: `MoveByAction` in Scene2D moves the actor by `(dx, dy)` over `duration` seconds. When `act(dt)` is called, it accumulates time and moves the actor proportionally. Once the accumulated time reaches `duration`, the action completes and is REDACTED-removed.

